1
00:00:31,520 --> 00:00:32,959
Good morning, students.

2
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:34,359
Today we will announce,

3
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:36,679
the format of our second exam.

4
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:37,680
Students will play

5
00:00:37,681 --> 00:00:39,479
the Perfect Partners group game,

6
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:41,720
to find their partner for the next round.

7
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:44,039
Based on the rankings from the last exam,

8
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:44,920
the top four students

9
00:00:44,921 --> 00:00:46,959
will go to the next room one by one

10
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:48,399
to answer multiple-choice questions.

11
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:50,679
Among the remaining students, whoever wants to team up with them,

12
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:52,559
must guess their answer.

13
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:56,239
When the answers are revealed, a match means the two students successfully team up.

14
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:58,479
If multiple people choose the same student, they can choose one in return.

15
00:00:58,480 --> 00:01:01,239
If no one picks or they refuse, they sit out.

16
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:03,840
The last ones left will team up freely.

17
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:08,040
We'll start with Bai Guanyu, who has the most credits.

18
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:17,079
If you could choose freely,

19
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:18,399
would you want to be first,

20
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:20,560
middle, or last in your family or group?

21
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:21,959
A. The eldest.

22
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:23,679
B. In the middle.

23
00:01:23,680 --> 00:01:25,640
C. Benjamin.

24
00:01:29,960 --> 00:01:31,679
Anyone willing to team up with Bai,

25
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:33,040
